Assessment Framework

Determine whether each control should be classified as:

ITDMC (IT-Dependent Manual Control)
MAC (Manual-Automated Control)
ITDMC Definition

Classify as ITDMC when:

The control relies on system-generated reports
Data extracts
Dashboards
Alerts
Workflow notifications
Information from systems

AND

Risk mitigation is performed primarily by people through:
Review
Investigation
Validation
Approval
Reconciliation
Judgement
Follow-up

Technology supports the control but does not independently perform a risk-mitigating control activity.

Automated reports, dashboards, data retrieval and workflow routing do not make a control MAC.

MAC Definition

Classify as MAC only when:

A risk-mitigating control activity is explicitly performed automatically through:

Business rule validation
Automated calculations
System-enforced restrictions
Automated monitoring
Automated exception detection
Automated matching
Automated reconciliation
Automated approval logic
Automated preventative controls

AND

A manual risk-mitigating activity also exists.

Both manual and automated activities must contribute to mitigating the risk.

Critical Analysis Rules
Control Activities

Risk-mitigating activities.

Examples:

Automated exception detection
Automated validation
Automated matching
Automated reconciliation
Manual review
Manual approval
Manual investigation
Process Steps

Operational activities that do not mitigate risk.

Examples:

Running reports
Downloading reports
Extracting data
Accessing systems
Generating dashboards

Do not classify as MAC solely because systems are used.

